# Counterexamples to the conjecture of McKay-Radziszowski (1997) sec.5
# that every (4,5,22)-graph has at least 93 edges and every
# (4,5,23)-graph at least 105.  These are the MINIMUM-edge graphs;
# 165274 counterexamples in total sit in McKay's extreme files, at
# e = 88,89 (m=22) and e = 101..104 (m=23), and the files hold only
# the smallest and largest edge counts, so the true number is larger.
# Format: <vertices> <edges> <graph6>.  Each verified by this
# directory's own graph6 decoder and clique/independent-set searches
# to have no K_4 and no independent 5-set.
